{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"3bf51904-8ac3-4fcb-841a-f19496ae0e95","agentId":"a2423e7f952588316","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes, no web browsing or searching. Memory on this PC is low: at most two CDP screenshots (job page 1400px dark, job page 400px), always kill Edge via cuore/tests/_edge_cleanup.py. Token-efficient: edit CSS mainly; read only the template regions you change; 4 checks; report under 100 words. Files: cuore/web/static/cuore.css (append a marked \"Emphasis pass\" section overriding the Marque theme section; do not rewrite earlier rules), cuore/web/templates/_verdict_card.html, _vbar.html (hero), _flow_bar.html, job.html (step headings and one-line step summaries only), cuore/tests/check_theme.py (adjust/extend to 4 checks).\n\nRepo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. Benchmark: a Ferrari model page: true black background, white text, one huge statement per section, key figures shown very large with small uppercase labels beneath, generous vertical space, red used only for the primary action, everything else quiet. The owner says CUORE today is hard to read, lacks emphasis, and is a wash of grey.\n\nDo: (1) Contrast: dark palette becomes true black (#000 / #0a0a0a surfaces), primary text #fff, secondary text a clear light grey (#b8bec4 or lighter), hairlines #2a2a2a; keep the light theme usable. (2) Readability: body 17px, line-height 1.6, text blocks max-width 72ch; headings light weight but large (page title 40px desktop / 30px phone; step headings 26/22px). (3) Hero (_vbar.html): below the car name, show the verdict as the headline (state in 44px+ uppercase with the amber/green/red colour, the one sentence in 20px), then a KEY FIGURES row of up to four big numbers (36px) with small uppercase labels: open codes (from view.code_counts if available, else from bar), days since last clear (view.verdict.cleared_at), km, fuel at last code set with \"in/out of 15-85 % window\" (from the first freeze frame flag if available); only render figures whose data exists; degrade silently otherwise (the vbar is included on pages without `view`: guard with `view is defined`). (4) Steps on job.html: each step heading becomes \"N  TITLE\" large; directly under it a one-line status in 20px light text derived from the flow state (`flow_state_for(vin)` global: that step's why) e.g. \"Not yet: no readiness read since the clear\"; details below unchanged. (5) Emphasis: the flow bar's primary button is the only filled red element; verdict chip colour by state; flagged freeze-frame values in amber; remove borders from chips except status chips; reduce chip font to 12px uppercase tracked; panels lose boxes and use whitespace plus one hairline. (6) Keep: 44px targets, status colours only for status, no CDN, print.css untouched. Checks: body computed font-size >= 17px; hero shows the verdict state text on the job and dossier pages; key figures row renders at least two figures for VIN ZASFAKPN5J7B88115; no horizontal overflow at 400px on the job page. Look at the two screenshots once; adjust until it reads bold and clear."},"uuid":"285afc04-7039-41a3-8b66-49ca93725d6f","timestamp":"2026-10-08T11:34:59.831Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
