{"parentUuid":"da0cb217-890a-4f0e-8a90-2d2cb10de270","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2423e7f952588316","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfpmFFnpTxmEeYuDeeBoe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No leftover debug code. Clean final state, all checks passing, no stray Edge processes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":272240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":430,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8ad0dbe7-9dd9-4b71-a923-cfa9eeded0d5","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfpmFFTUarAYqnbEhMFe2","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c5972504-8c4a-42bb-b671-e40d13ae7688","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:23:35.302Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"c5972504-8c4a-42bb-b671-e40d13ae7688","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2423e7f952588316","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfpmFFnpTxmEeYuDeeBoe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LNhoLtLr41KELd82fcCXG9","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Emphasis pass shipped and verified. All 4 checks pass (plus 2 screenshot-capture assertions, 6 total), 0 stray Edge processes left, screenshots reviewed once.\n\nChanges:\n- cuore/web/static/cuore.css: appended \"Emphasis pass\" section (after Marque theme, nothing earlier rewritten) — true-black dark palette (#000/#0a0a0a/#fff/#b8bec4/#2a2a2a hairlines, light theme untouched since it's set via higher-specificity selectors), body 17px, 72ch text caps, large light-weight headings (h1 40/30px, .section-h/.step-title 26/22px with a thin marque-accent rule underneath), hero band (38vh/30vh, gradient to black, name 56/36px, marque tagline, verdict headline 44px+ colored by state, key-figures row 36px/28px), .chip bumped to 12px uppercase tracked.\n- cuore/web/templates/_vbar.html: hero now shows the marque tagline (Alfa: \"Passion and the joy of driving\"; other marques degrade silently — no copy was invented for them), the verdict headline + one-sentence summary, and a key-figures row (open codes from view.code_counts.active, odometer from bar.odo_last, fuel-at-code-set with an in/out-of-window amber flag from the first freeze frame) — all guarded by `view is defined`.\n- cuore/web/templates/job.html: added a `step_oneliner(n)` macro reading `flow.steps`, called after each of the 12 step headings for a one-line \"Not yet: <why>\" status.\n- cuore/tests/check_theme.py: rewritten to the 4 specified checks (body font-size >=17px; hero verdict-state text present on job+dossier; key-figures row >=2 for the Stelvio VIN; no 400px overflow on job), capped at 2 screenshots (job_1400 dark, job_400).\n\nOne real bug found and fixed, worth flagging: this headless Edge build silently drops every even-numbered bare `:root { }`-only-custom-properties rule in cuore.css (confirmed via CDP cssRules introspection, not a cascade/specificity issue — a pre-existing `--fam-*` block was already silently dead because of it). Worked around with a documented no-op decoy `:root` rule placed just before the real one so it lands on an odd occurrence and survives; explained in a comment in cuore.css. Worth a look if this build is ever upgraded.\n\nScreenshots in scratchpad: job_1400.png (forced dark, confirmed true #000 by pixel sample), job_400.png (natural/light theme, confirms light still usable, no overflow)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":272240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":430,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LNhoLtLr41KELd82fcCXG9":{"message":"Emphasis pass shipped and verified. All 4 checks pass (plus 2 screenshot-capture assertions, 6 total), 0 stray Edge processes left, screenshots reviewed once.\n\nChanges:\n- cuore/web/static/cuore.css: appended \"Emphasis pass\" section (after Marque theme, nothing earlier rewritten) — true-black dark palette (#000/#0a0a0a/#fff/#b8bec4/#2a2a2a hairlines, light theme untouched since it's set via higher-specificity selectors), body 17px, 72ch text caps, large light-weight headings (h1 40/30px, .section-h/.step-title 26/22px with a thin marque-accent rule underneath), hero band (38vh/30vh, gradient to black, name 56/36px, marque tagline, verdict headline 44px+ colored by state, key-figures row 36px/28px), .chip bumped to 12px uppercase tracked.\n- cuore/web/templates/_vbar.html: hero now shows the marque tagline (Alfa: \"Passion and the joy of driving\"; other marques degrade silently — no copy was invented for them), the verdict headline + one-sentence summary, and a key-figures row (open codes from view.code_counts.active, odometer from bar.odo_last, fuel-at-code-set with an in/out-of-window amber flag from the first freeze frame) — all guarded by `view is defined`.\n- cuore/web/templates/job.html: added a `step_oneliner(n)` macro reading `flow.steps`, called after each of the 12 step headings for a one-line \"Not yet: <why>\" status.\n- cuore/tests/check_theme.py: rewritten to the 4 specified checks (body font-size >=17px; hero verdict-state text present on job+dossier; key-figures row >=2 for the Stelvio VIN; no 400px overflow on job), capped at 2 screenshots (job_1400 dark, job_400).\n\nOne real bug found and fixed, worth flagging: this headless Edge build silently drops every even-numbered bare `:root { }`-only-custom-properties rule in cuore.css (confirmed via CDP cssRules introspection, not a cascade/specificity issue — a pre-existing `--fam-*` block was already silently dead because of it). Worked around with a documented no-op decoy `:root` rule placed just before the real one so it lands on an odd occurrence and survives; explained in a comment in cuore.css. Worth a look if this build is ever upgraded.\n\nScreenshots in scratchpad: job_1400.png (forced dark, confirmed true #000 by pixel sample), job_400.png (natural/light theme, confirms light still usable, no overflow)."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8ad0dbe7-9dd9-4b71-a923-cfa9eeded0d5","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfpmFFTUarAYqnbEhMFe2","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b7cee6af-86cb-4dfa-9721-de558d21fbf8","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:23:45.530Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
